{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":50596,"duration_api_ms":47863,"ttft_ms":6952,"ttft_stream_ms":2520,"time_to_request_ms":176,"num_turns":10,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"This repo has no Docker/CI/CD pipeline files and deploys via Vercel's git integration with environment config stored in Vercel project settings (Production/Preview), not in-repo. My infra work for status-page is limited to: wiring the environment/version signal the status endpoint will report, deciding how build-time metadata (version, commit SHA, environment name) is injected into the Next.js app, and optionally hooking the endpoint into uptime/observability. The actual API route handler and status UI page are application code owned by other roles.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"Vercel project environment variables (Production/Preview)\",\n    \"Build-time version/commit metadata injection (no existing mechanism found)\",\n    \"Observability/uptime monitoring (none currently configured in-repo)\",\n    \".env.example documentation of any new env vars\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Define and document how the running environment is identified (e.g. expose NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL's existing Production/Preview/local distinction, or add a new APP_ENV/VERCEL_ENV-derived value) so the status endpoint can report it without hardcoding. Vercel auto-injects VERCEL_ENV ('production'|'preview'|'development') and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA server-side by default — recommend reading those directly rather than adding new secrets.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Determine the backend version source: use package.json's \\\"version\\\" field (currently 0.1.0) and/or VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA for build identification. No existing versioning scheme was found in the repo, so confirm with the backend owner which value the /api/status endpoint should return.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the new/used env vars (if any new ones are introduced) in .env.example, following the existing pattern that separates local/.env.local, Vercel Preview, and Vercel Production values.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-4\",\n      \"description\": \"(Optional, flag as a question) Decide whether an external uptime monitor should poll the new status endpoint. No observability/monitoring stack currently exists in this repo or its docs, so this would be a net-new integration requiring explicit user authorization before wiring any third-party service or secret.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-1 (dependency, not mine)\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the actual API route (e.g. app/api/status/route.ts) that returns availability, version, and environment as JSON. Owned by backend/app engineer.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\", \"infra-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"frontend-1 (dependency, not mine)\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the user-facing status page (app/ route) that fetches and renders the status endpoint's data. Owned by frontend engineer.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"frontend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"docs-1 (dependency, not mine)\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the new endpoint/page per the project's docs conventions (docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md, relevant engineering guide) and ensure npm run docs:check passes.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend-engineer or frontend-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1\", \"frontend-1\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Environment value should be sourced from process.env.VERCEL_ENV (falls back to 'development' locally) rather than a new custom variable, unless the team wants a distinct app-level label.\",\n    \"Version value should be sourced from package.json \\\"version\\\" and/or process.env.VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (both are read server-side only; VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA is not available in local dev).\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"process.env.VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA and VERCEL_ENV are undefined in local dev (npm run dev) and in some CI contexts — the endpoint must handle missing values gracefully rather than throwing.\",\n    \"No CI/CD pipeline exists in this repo today (no .github/workflows, no vercel.json) — introducing monitoring/CI hooks for this feature would be new infrastructure scope beyond the feature itself and needs explicit confirmation before adding.\",\n    \"If 'API availability' is meant to reflect Supabase connectivity, the status endpoint would need to perform a live check against Supabase, which touches credentials/config (lib/supabase/server.ts) — confirm this is in scope before any implementation, since it affects what the endpoint depends on at runtime.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Not owned by this role directly, but infra should ensure: env var fallbacks (missing VERCEL_ENV/VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA in local/test runs) don't break the endpoint — flag this as a required test case for whoever implements the route.\",\n    \"No test is needed for infra config itself since no new infra code/files are proposed beyond documentation.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Does 'API availability' mean the Next.js server is reachable (trivial, always true if the route responds), or does it require an active check against Supabase/other dependencies? This changes scope significantly.\",\n    \"Should 'backend version' be the npm package version (0.1.0), the git commit SHA, or both?\",\n    \"Is any external uptime/monitoring integration (e.g. a third-party status checker hitting this endpoint) actually wanted, or is this purely an in-app display feature? No such integration exists today.\",\n    \"Should the environment label distinguish Supabase dev vs prod (as the project does for env vars) separately from Vercel's Production/Preview/Development, since those two axes aren't always identical per .env.example's comments?\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c970bdf9-6283-423a-90c0-187fb39e1a72","total_cost_usd":0.3622158,"usage":{"input_tokens":18151,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29785,"cache_read_input_tokens":236326,"output_tokens":3877,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29785,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":52386,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":18151,"outputTokens":3877,"cacheReadInputTokens":236326,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29785,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3622158,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ed92808d-043d-4126-8034-c1cdaae859c8"}
